\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Spinodal character and equilibrium two-phase compositions as a function of temperature for the binary Nb$_{50}$V$_{50}$ and ternary Nb$_{50}$Hf$_5$V$_{45}$ BCC\textsubscript  {A2} alloys. Signs of the diagonal Hessian elements indicate whether each element is individually unstable ($H_{ii} < 0$, driving force) or stable ($H_{ii} > 0$, spectator/stiffener). $H_{\rm  V}$ is derived from the reduced Hessian via $H_{\rm  V} = H_{\rm  Nb} + H_{\rm  Hf} + 2H_{\rm  Nb,Hf}$. }}{22}{table.caption.78}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:spinodal_regimes}{{4}{22}{Spinodal character and equilibrium two-phase compositions as a function of temperature for the binary Nb$_{50}$V$_{50}$ and ternary Nb$_{50}$Hf$_5$V$_{45}$ BCC\textsubscript {A2} alloys. Signs of the diagonal Hessian elements indicate whether each element is individually unstable ($H_{ii} < 0$, driving force) or stable ($H_{ii} > 0$, spectator/stiffener). $H_{\rm V}$ is derived from the reduced Hessian via $H_{\rm V} = H_{\rm Nb} + H_{\rm Hf} + 2H_{\rm Nb,Hf}$}{table.caption.78}{}}
